<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35437" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-saepe</span></b> , adv., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very often</i>, <i>very frequently</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quod persaepe fit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 20, 75</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frons, oculi, voltus persaepe mentiuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q. Fr. 1, 1, 5, § 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">persaepe velut qui Junonis sacra ferret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 3, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				A. P. 349</span></i>.—In tmesi: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per pol saepe peccas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 2, 6, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
